<h2>Topic 1: Introduction to Life Insurance</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Define life insurance, explain why people buy it, distinguish life vs general.</p>
<p>Life insurance is a promise: you pay premiums, the insurer pays a sum assured if you die, or if you survive to a date, depending on the policy. It protects the people who depend on you.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Why buy it:</b> 1. Protect family - if breadwinner dies, family still has money. 2. Save - endowment builds savings. 3. Retirement - annuity gives income. 4. Loan - bank wants cover before lending.</p><p><b>Life vs General:</b> Life is long-term, pays on death / survival, no indemnity - sum assured is agreed. General is 1 year, pays loss, indemnity applies.</p></div>
