<h2>Topic 2: Types of Life Insurance</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain term, whole life, endowment, annuity, unit-linked, give cover and best for whom.</p>
<p>Always answer: <b>What it pays + When + Best for whom + One disadvantage</b>.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Term Assurance:</b> Pays only if die within term, e.g. 10 years. Cheapest. No payout if survive.</p><p><b>Whole Life:</b> Pays whenever you die. Most expensive, covers whole life.</p><p><b>Endowment:</b> Pays if die within term OR survive to end. Saving + protection.</p><p><b>Annuity:</b> You pay lump sum, insurer pays regular income for life / fixed years. For retirement.</p><p><b>Unit-Linked:</b> Premium invested in funds. Value goes up and down.</p></div>
