<h2>Topic 3: Life Tables and Mortality</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain life table, read lx, dx, qx, px, calculate survival and death probabilities.</p>
<p>A life table shows, for each age x: lx = number alive at age x, dx = number dying between x and x+1, qx = probability of dying, px = probability of surviving.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Formulas:</b> qx = dx / lx. px = 1 - qx = (lx+1) / lx.</p><p><b>Example:</b> l30 = 100000, d30 = 500. q30 = 500 / 100000 = 0.005. p30 = 0.995. So a 30-year-old has 0.5% chance of dying before 31, 99.5% chance of surviving.</p></div><p><b>Exam trick:</b> Always show dx / lx, not just the answer.</p>
