<h2>Topic 4: Premiums and Reserves</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain premium, calculate expected claims and premium, explain reserve.</p>
<p>Premium is the price. It must cover expected claims + expenses + profit, with a margin for safety.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Expected claims:</b> Lives x qx x Sum Assured. Example: 1000 lives, q=0.005, sum 1000000. Expected deaths = 5. Expected claims = 5 x 1000000 = 5000000.</p><p><b>Premium per person:</b> If expenses 500000, profit 500000: Total needed = 6000000. Premium per person = 6000000 / 1000 = 6000.</p><p><b>Reserve:</b> Money set aside today for future claims. Reserve = PV Future Benefits - PV Future Premiums. If reserves are too low, company fails.</p></div>
