<h2>Topic 5: Underwriting and Claims in Life Insurance</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain underwriting, explain factors, explain claims process, explain why claims are refused.</p>
<p>Underwriting is checking risk before accepting. Claims is paying when the event happens.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Underwriting checks:</b> Age, Health, Smoking, Occupation, Family history, Medical exam, Financial - can you afford premium? Is sum assured reasonable?</p><p><b>Outcomes:</b> Accept at normal rate, Accept with loading (higher premium), Accept with exclusion, Decline.</p><p><b>Claims:</b> Notify, Death certificate / proof, Policy document, Check: was premium paid? Was cause covered? Was there fraud / non-disclosure? Pay to beneficiary.</p></div>
